    "21. Return of Pallets.",
    "Pallets or similar articles of transport supplied by or on behalf of the Carrier shall be returned to the Carrier in the same order and condition as handed over to the Merchant, normal wear and tear excepted, with interiors clean and within the time prescribed in the Carrier's tariff or elsewhere.",
    "The Merchant shall be liable to the Carrier for any loss, damage to, or delay, including demurrage and detention incurred by or sustained to containers, pallets or similar articles of transport during the period between handing over to the Merchant and return to the Carrier.",
    "22. ANEMOS",
    "(a) The carrying-vessel shall be a vessel whose main propulsion is  wind power.",
    "(b) The Carrier shall offer to the Merchant ANEMOS Scheme, which is a collective trademark (class 39, APPENDICE XXX) that certifies a product has been shipped on board a wind powered vessel.",
    "(c)ANEMOS provides a tracking solution of the Vessel(s) and the Goods, and covers engine utilisation, CO2 emissions, CO2 emissions per unit of goods transported, as well as photographs, films, and all other contents which document the passage.",
    "(d) ANEMOS is materialized by a label applied onto each sail-transported product, which provides a visual differentiation to the end customer. The purpose of ANEMOS is to protect both the end customer (from greenwashing) and the cargo-Owners (from greenwashing competitors) in their commitment to reduce the carbon footprint of their maritime logistics, in full transparency and integrity.",
    "(e)The Carrier largely encourages the Merchant to certify their sail cargo crossings with ANEMOS, and to cooperate with other non-competing cargo-Owners in promoting and defending the ANEMOS label.",
